{
  "_id": "leviticus19",
  "book": {
    "_id": "leviticus",
    "title": "Leviticus",
    "titleShort": "Lev.",
    "titleOfficial": "",
    "subtitle": "",
    "summary": "",
    "chapterDelineation": "Chapter"
  },
  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Leviticus",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 19,
    "summary": "Israel is commanded: Be holy, live righteously, love your neighbor, and keep the commandments—The Lord reveals and reaffirms sundry laws and commandments—Enchantments, wizardry, prostitution, and all evil practices are forbidden.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "And the Lord spake unto Moses, saying,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Speak unto all the congregation of the children of Israel, and say unto them, Ye shall be holy: for I the Lord your God am holy.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 90,
            "end": 94,
            "text": "OR saints or holy ones. Josh. 24:19; Isa. 5:16; D&C 82:14. TG God, the Standard of Righteousness; Holiness."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 120,
            "end": 122
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Ye shall fear every man his mother, and his father, and keep my sabbaths: I am the Lord your God.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 64,
            "end": 72,
            "text": "D&C 59:9."
          },
          {
            "start": 83,
            "end": 87,
            "text": "Lev. 20:8."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 76,
            "end": 78
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Turn ye not unto idols, nor make to yourselves molten gods: I am the Lord your God.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 17,
            "end": 22,
            "text": "Judg. 17:3 (3–4); 2 Ne. 9:37; D&C 1:16."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 62,
            "end": 64
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And if ye offer a sacrifice of peace offerings unto the Lord, ye shall offer it at your own will.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 71,
            "end": 76,
            "text": "TG Sacrifice."
          },
          {
            "start": 92,
            "end": 96,
            "text": "Moro. 7:6."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "It shall be eaten the same day ye offer it, and on the morrow: and if ought remain until the third day, it shall be burnt in the fire.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And if it be eaten at all on the third day, it is abominable; it shall not be accepted.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 50,
            "end": 60,
            "text": "Lev. 7:18; Ezek. 4:14."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 47,
            "end": 49
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Therefore every one that eateth it shall bear his iniquity, because he hath profaned the hallowed thing of the Lord: and that soul shall be cut off from among his people.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 41,
            "end": 45,
            "text": "Lev. 5:1 (1–6)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 10,
            "end": 19
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And when ye reap the harvest of your land, thou shalt not wholly reap the corners of thy field, neither shalt thou gather the gleanings of thy harvest.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 21,
            "end": 28,
            "text": "TG Harvest."
          },
          {
            "start": 65,
            "end": 69,
            "text": "Ruth 2:2 (2, 12)."
          },
          {
            "start": 126,
            "end": 135,
            "text": "Ruth 2:8 (2–9); Mosiah 4:26; D&C 42:31."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And thou shalt not glean thy vineyard, neither shalt thou gather every grape of thy vineyard; thou shalt leave them for the poor and stranger: I am the Lord your God.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 124,
            "end": 128,
            "text": "TG Charity; Poor; Welfare."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 65,
            "end": 70
          },
          {
            "start": 145,
            "end": 147
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Ye shall not steal, neither deal falsely, neither lie one to another.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 13,
            "end": 18,
            "text": "TG Stealing."
          },
          {
            "start": 28,
            "end": 32,
            "text": "D&C 136:25."
          },
          {
            "start": 50,
            "end": 53,
            "text": "TG Lying."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And ye shall not swear by my name falsely, neither shalt thou profane the name of thy God: I am the Lord.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 17,
            "end": 22,
            "text": "TG Swearing."
          },
          {
            "start": 34,
            "end": 41,
            "text": "TG Honesty."
          },
          {
            "start": 62,
            "end": 69,
            "text": "TG Profanity."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 93,
            "end": 95
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Thou shalt not defraud thy neighbour, neither rob him: the wages of him that is hired shall not abide with thee all night until the morning.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 15,
            "end": 22,
            "text": "Deut. 24:15. TG Fraud."
          },
          {
            "start": 27,
            "end": 36,
            "text": "TG Neighbor."
          },
          {
            "start": 59,
            "end": 64,
            "text": "TG Wages."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 50,
            "end": 54
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Thou shalt not curse the deaf, nor put a stumblingblock before the blind, but shalt fear thy God: I am the Lord.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 15,
            "end": 20,
            "text": "TG Curse."
          },
          {
            "start": 25,
            "end": 29,
            "text": "TG Compassion."
          },
          {
            "start": 41,
            "end": 55,
            "text": "Rom. 14:13."
          },
          {
            "start": 67,
            "end": 72,
            "text": "Deut. 27:18."
          },
          {
            "start": 103,
            "end": 111,
            "text": "HEB Jehovah. Note that this phrase occurs fifteen times like a seal of authority upon each of these statutes."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 100,
            "end": 102
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Ye shall do no unrighteousness in judgment: thou shalt not respect the person of the poor, nor honour the person of the mighty: but in righteousness shalt thou judge thy neighbour.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 15,
            "end": 30,
            "text": "HEB injustice. Ex. 23:3 (1–3)."
          },
          {
            "start": 34,
            "end": 42,
            "text": "TG Judgment."
          },
          {
            "start": 59,
            "end": 66,
            "text": "IE show unjust favoritism either to the humble or the mighty. Deut. 1:17; D&C 38:25 (25–27)."
          },
          {
            "start": 135,
            "end": 148,
            "text": "TG Righteousness."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 128,
            "end": 131
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Thou shalt not go up and down as a talebearer among thy people: neither shalt thou stand against the blood of thy neighbour: I am the Lord.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 35,
            "end": 45,
            "text": "TG Gossip; Honesty."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 30,
            "end": 32
          },
          {
            "start": 127,
            "end": 129
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Thou shalt not hate thy brother in thine heart: thou shalt in any wise rebuke thy neighbour, and not suffer sin upon him.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 4,
            "text": "IE Though you may reprove a neighbor and not tolerate his sin, do not hate him. Jacob 2:7; D&C 121:43."
          },
          {
            "start": 41,
            "end": 46,
            "text": "TG Hardheartedness."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Thou shalt not avenge, nor bear any grudge against the children of thy people, but thou shalt love thy neighbour as thyself: I am the Lord.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 15,
            "end": 21,
            "text": "TG Forbear; Retribution."
          },
          {
            "start": 36,
            "end": 42,
            "text": "TG Malice."
          },
          {
            "start": 94,
            "end": 98,
            "text": "TG Charity; Love."
          },
          {
            "start": 103,
            "end": 112,
            "text": "TG Fellowshipping; Neighbor."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 127,
            "end": 129
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Ye shall keep my statutes. Thou shalt not let thy cattle gender with a diverse kind: thou shalt not sow thy field with mingled seed: neither shall a garment mingled of linen and woollen come upon thee.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 27,
            "end": 31,
            "text": "Note that these laws are in harmony with the other admonitions to keep things pure and in proper use. TG Separation."
          },
          {
            "start": 119,
            "end": 126,
            "text": "Deut. 22:9."
          },
          {
            "start": 157,
            "end": 164,
            "text": "Deut. 22:11."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And whosoever lieth carnally with a woman, that is a bondmaid, betrothed to an husband, and not at all redeemed, nor freedom given her; she shall be scourged; they shall not be put to death, because she was not free.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 76,
            "end": 86,
            "text": "HEB a man."
          },
          {
            "start": 136,
            "end": 157,
            "text": "HEB there shall be an investigation or inquisition."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 48,
            "end": 50
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And he shall bring his trespass offering unto the Lord, unto the door of the tabernacle of the congregation, even a ram for a trespass offering.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 109,
            "end": 113
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And the priest shall make an atonement for him with the ram of the trespass offering before the Lord for his sin which he hath done: and the sin which he hath done shall be forgiven him.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 173,
            "end": 181,
            "text": "TG Forgive."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And when ye shall come into the land, and shall have planted all manner of trees for food, then ye shall count the fruit thereof as uncircumcised: three years shall it be as uncircumcised unto you: it shall not be eaten of.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "But in the fourth year all the fruit thereof shall be holy to praise the Lord withal.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 78,
            "end": 85
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And in the fifth year shall ye eat of the fruit thereof, that it may yield unto you the increase thereof: I am the Lord your God.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 108,
            "end": 110
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Ye shall not eat any thing with the blood: neither shall ye use enchantment, nor observe times.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 36,
            "end": 41,
            "text": "TG Blood, Eating of."
          },
          {
            "start": 43,
            "end": 50,
            "text": "HEB you shall not divine or use sorcery."
          },
          {
            "start": 64,
            "end": 75,
            "text": "2 Kgs. 21:6; 2 Ne. 10:15; 26:22 (22–23)."
          },
          {
            "start": 81,
            "end": 88,
            "text": "Deut. 18:14; Isa. 47:13 (13–15)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 17,
            "end": 26
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Ye shall not round the corners of your heads, neither shalt thou mar the corners of thy beard.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 13,
            "end": 18,
            "text": "IE by cutting the forelocks of the hair of the head. Lev. 21:5."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Ye shall not make any cuttings in your flesh for the dead, nor print any marks upon you: I am the Lord.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 22,
            "end": 30,
            "text": "1 Kgs. 18:28. TG Mourning."
          },
          {
            "start": 39,
            "end": 44,
            "text": "TG Body, Sanctity of."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 91,
            "end": 93
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Do not prostitute thy daughter, to cause her to be a whore; lest the land fall to whoredom, and the land become full of wickedness.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 7,
            "end": 17,
            "text": "Deut. 23:17 (17–18)."
          },
          {
            "start": 82,
            "end": 90,
            "text": "TG Whore."
          },
          {
            "start": 120,
            "end": 130,
            "text": "HEB lewdness."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Ye shall keep my sabbaths, and reverence my sanctuary: I am the Lord.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 17,
            "end": 25,
            "text": "Lev. 23:3."
          },
          {
            "start": 31,
            "end": 40,
            "text": "TG Reverence."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 57,
            "end": 59
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Regard not them that have familiar spirits, neither seek after wizards, to be defiled by them: I am the Lord your God.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 6,
            "text": "HEB Do not turn to magic or necromancy."
          },
          {
            "start": 26,
            "end": 34,
            "text": "TG Spirits, Evil or Unclean."
          },
          {
            "start": 35,
            "end": 42,
            "text": "TG Sorcery."
          },
          {
            "start": 63,
            "end": 70,
            "text": "TG Superstitions."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 97,
            "end": 99
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Thou shalt rise up before the hoary head, and honour the face of the old man, and fear thy God: I am the Lord.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 11,
            "end": 15,
            "text": "HEB rise before the face of old age."
          },
          {
            "start": 30,
            "end": 35,
            "text": "Prov. 20:29."
          },
          {
            "start": 46,
            "end": 52,
            "text": "TG Courtesy; Family, Children, Duties of; Respect."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 98,
            "end": 100
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And if a stranger sojourn with thee in your land, ye shall not vex him.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 63,
            "end": 66,
            "text": "HEB oppress."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "But the stranger that dwelleth with you shall be unto you as one born among you, and thou shalt love him as thyself; for ye were strangers in the land of Egypt: I am the Lord your God.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 16,
            "text": "TG Fellowshipping; Stranger."
          },
          {
            "start": 58,
            "end": 60,
            "text": "HEB as a citizen of yours."
          },
          {
            "start": 96,
            "end": 100,
            "text": "Deut. 10:19. TG Love."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 3
          },
          {
            "start": 163,
            "end": 165
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Ye shall do no unrighteousness in judgment, in meteyard, in weight, or in measure.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 15,
            "end": 30,
            "text": "HEB injustice."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Just balances, just weights, a just ephah, and a just hin, shall ye have: I am the Lord your God, which brought you out of the land of Egypt.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 20,
            "end": 27,
            "text": "Deut. 25:13."
          },
          {
            "start": 36,
            "end": 41,
            "text": "Deut. 25:15 (14–15); Ezek. 45:10; Amos 8:5."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 76,
            "end": 78
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Therefore shall ye observe all my statutes, and all my judgments, and do them: I am the Lord.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 81,
            "end": 83
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      }
    ]
  },
  "nextChapterId": "leviticus20",
  "prevChapterId": "leviticus18",
  "volume": {
    "_id": "oldtestament",
    "title": "Old Testament",
    "titleShort": "OT",
    "titleOfficial": "The Old Testament"
  }
}